{{!
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  phlox default template — language-independent
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  Reproduces the section grammar described in [[Output Writers]] (wiki).
  Loaded automatically when AbstractRenderContext.getTemplate() is null.

  All literal strings route through {{label:...}}, so this single template
  serves every language phlox supports — adding a new locale means dropping
  in a new phlox-labels_<lang>.properties in phlox-api, never a new template.

  Conventions used here:
  - Sections wrapped in {{?BG-X}} or {{?BT-X}} vanish when their data is
    empty; no manual whitespace cleanup needed.
  - GFM tables are used wherever the source has a list shape: invoice lines,
    allowances, charges, VAT breakdowns, document totals, supporting docs.
  - {{class:...}} hints flag rows or blocks where the HTML side wants a CSS
    class and the PDF side wants a fill colour from the style map.
  - Inside each section, the comment block above lists every BG/BT used.
    Format: "BT-N  BT name (cardinality)" — see [[Domain Model]] for the
    full inventory.
}}

{{!
  ─── Logo ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Optional; supplied via RenderContext.setLogo(PhloxAttachment).
  Resolved via the "attachment:logo" image URL scheme — see
  [[Template Language]] § Images.
}}
{{?logo}}![Logo](attachment:logo)

{{/logo}}
